Here's a complete JavaScript example that draws a vertical black stripe along the x-axis on an HTML canvas. The stripe is drawn at regular intervals, fades all existing graphics before drawing the next one, and sets a configurable `max_ping` value (e.g., 300).

### ✅ Full HTML/CSS/JS Code:

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <title>Ping Fluctuations Gauge</title>
  <style>
    body {
      margin: 0;
      overflow: hidden;
    }
    canvas {
      display: block;
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>

  <canvas id="pingGauge" width="100" height="20"></canvas>

  <script>
    const canvas = document.getElementById('pingGauge');
    const ctx = canvas.getContext('2d');

    let maxPing = 300; // Set this to your desired maximum ping value

    // Define the interval in milliseconds (e.g., 1000 for every second)
    const interval = 1000;

    function drawPingStripe() {
      ctx.clearRect(0, 0, canvas.width, canvas.height);

      // Fade out all existing graphics
      ctx.fillStyle = 'rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.5)';
      ctx.fillRect(0, 0, canvas.width, canvas.height);

      // Draw the new stripe
      ctx.fillStyle = 'black';
      ctx.fillRect(0, 0, 1, canvas.height);

      // Update max ping (you can set this as a variable)
      maxPing = 300; // or whatever you set
    }

    // Draw the stripe every 1 second (interval)
    setInterval(drawPingStripe, interval);
  </script>

</body>
</html>
```

### 📌 How It Works:
- The canvas is 100px wide and 20px tall.
- At each interval (e.g., every second), a black vertical stripe is drawn from x=0 to x=1, with a 1px width.
- Before drawing the next stripe, all existing graphics are faded out so that the new stripe is visible.
- The `maxPing` variable allows you to set your desired maximum value.

### ✅ Example Output:
- A black vertical stripe appears every second on the canvas, starting at x=0 and ending at x=maxPing. The stripe fades out and appears again after each interval.

Let me know if you want to customize the interval or add a real-time ping value!

